         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nThe first number of the numerical systems used nowadays around the world is the zero (0), which represents the idea of emptiness — of nothing. Zero is not merely an empty spot on the page: it is the number that tells us there is no quantity to count.\n\nAs a consequence of this, all the results of the multiplication table of zero can be reduced to one single number. In this class, we will learn the multiplication table of zero and discover why every one of its answers is the same.\n\nRemember from our previous classes: multiplying is a fast way of adding the same number many times. Keep that idea in mind, and the rule of the table of zero will feel natural.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
