               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### A Rule\n\nFrom the previous screen, we can observe that when working with multiplication tables, we are going to repeat the same task different times, changing only one value. As a consequence of this, we can create a general recipe for how to build each multiplication table.\n\nFor example, when working with the multiplication table of zero, we can define it as:\n\n**0 = 0 × N**",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "21bbcdd1-5f72-4a28-abec-44a2c209369c",
