               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this class, we learned the multiplication table of zero. We observed that, independent of the number we multiply by zero, the result will always be one single number: the zero.\n\nThis happens because we do not have objects to count. No matter how many groups we form, we keep counting nothing — and nothing is always zero.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
